{
    "background_story": "Promise was a proud and majestic horse with a shiny black coat and a spirited personality to match. She was a favorite among the riders at the local stable, known for her strength, agility, and gentle disposition. But what made Promise truly special was her role in the annual Renaissance fair. Every year, she would be adorned with intricate costumes and ornate saddles, her rider dressed in elaborate attire. The pi\u00e8ce de r\u00e9sistance was the delicate buckram fabric used to create the intricate designs on Promise's saddle and bridle. The stiff, woven fabric added a touch of elegance and sophistication to Promise's already regal appearance. As she pranced and danced through the fairgrounds, Promise was the epitome of poise and refinement, her buckram-adorned saddle sparkling in the sunlight.",
